Paramdex — third-party param definitions
========================================

Source:  https://github.com/soulsmods/Paramdex
Vendored: NR/Defs only (226 XML files)

What these are
--------------
Each file describes the byte layout of one of the game's param tables: for
every field, its offset, its type and its name. regulation.bin decrypts to a
set of binary tables whose rows are otherwise opaque blobs, so these layouts
are what make the data readable at all.

They contain no game content. There is no artwork, no text and no game data
here — only the schema describing where values sit.

What Nightreign Helper takes from them
--------------------------------------
The schema, and only the schema, for the 17 param tables it reads: roughly
1,384 field definitions. Everything built on top — what the fields mean,
which combine and how, the save file format, and the application itself — is
this project's own work and is covered by its MIT licence.

Licence position
----------------
Paramdex carries no licence file, so no licence is granted or implied by its
authors, and none is claimed here. It is included because the tool cannot
read the game without it and because redistributing it in this form is long-
standing practice among comparable open-source tools, notably DSMapStudio
and Smithbox.

If you are a Paramdex contributor and would prefer this project not
redistribute your work, please open an issue and it will be removed.

